#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046665} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406831} :activity/id #uuid "fa97339f-4dd8-5f3c-87ec-f76f876eeb93" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050164 :topic/id #uuid "32af04f7-8bd5-5a90-8e7c-6c111c983ee8" :topic/math-academy-id 1955} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406830 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338924 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0284616a-7c89-5ca0-af71-91a32977c6fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336059} {:answer/id #uuid "208d69f2-61c9-5cef-ae67-df4b82077458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "⟨0,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336345} {:answer/id #uuid "4733129a-0c72-56e1-9873-d6951efbe108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "⟨0,6,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336698} {:answer/id #uuid "54939340-4ca9-5a82-b24c-2542ed64af8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "⟨0,-6,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336820} {:answer/id #uuid "fb04c736-1e93-5392-937a-e6b52b89f395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "⟨0,-2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338240}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336059} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ee8ed97-cdf9-56b8-9f86-2a9258c8b74b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2d6bbe53-bb73-5d24-b77f-7c5fef3fe5bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-71220" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=-2.$ Given that the point $P(-2,-6,1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=\\frac{y-x}{\\sqrt{x(y+x)}}$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=-2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(-2,-6).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(-2,-6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-2,-6) & =\\frac{-6-(-2)}{\\sqrt{(-2)(-6+(-2))}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{\\sqrt{16}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{4} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(-2,-6) & ={f}_{y}(-2,-6)(y-(-6)) \\\\ z-1 & =-1(y+6) \\\\ z-1 & =-y-6 \\\\ z & =-y-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-2,-6,1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=-y-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=-2,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=-y-5$ (or $y+z+5=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $⟨0,-1,1⟩.$"} :step/id #uuid "1cff8fcf-d3d9-54eb-b0e4-27eb94529c2d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406832}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406831 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323798 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "204035e4-46d4-534d-ba05-15ce0e052f85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=4y+8\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321393} {:answer/id #uuid "5b70aad1-ccca-5779-affa-e5700fd0cc6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=-4x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321874} {:answer/id #uuid "7510c1fa-11fc-530d-ac02-4cbbe0845097" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=-4y+8\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322065} {:answer/id #uuid "85c6028a-d0f8-58ef-9cb9-0c6994f1659c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=4x+8\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322212} {:answer/id #uuid "9cadbd18-60fa-56f2-aef5-823c9dd90a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=4y-8\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322388}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186322065} :answer-field/id #uuid "57b4da25-e31a-52b9-9b49-54d616020d35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "daecb367-4754-591f-93db-eaa083b20ffe" :question/math-academy-id "q-36301" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=-2.$ Given that the point $P(-2,0,8)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+4y+x$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=-2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(-2,0,8)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(-2,0)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(-2,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(-2,0)} & =(-2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+4(0)+(-2) \\\\  & =-2-2 \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(-2,0)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(-2,0)}(y-0) \\\\ z-8 & =-4(y-0) \\\\ z & =-4y+8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-2,0,8)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=-4y+8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1dbe7c48-28df-580f-b8a4-86e8677a0881" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406830}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406832 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406829 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "047539be-1b12-5b55-a1be-3e4cf9e127fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "⟨1,0,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406823} {:answer/id #uuid "43cdbb4c-51d2-5f61-9d40-d04783c14422" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "⟨1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406824} {:answer/id #uuid "60dae67c-4a44-58da-b15e-79beacb9c712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "⟨1,0,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406825} {:answer/id #uuid "652341d7-abb3-51cc-926c-835644238288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406826} {:answer/id #uuid "e3f93202-6d15-5d8b-9e8d-6d60c947ab0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "⟨-2,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406827}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406824} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b52ca0e-0824-536f-99e9-5701cb39c975" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "320a3cd2-acfa-559d-b91b-9bfb6f0a3cde" :question/math-academy-id "q-71231" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Given that the point $P(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4},0)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $y=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ at $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & ={f}_{x}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4})(x-1) \\\\ z-0 & =1(x-1) \\\\ z & =x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4},0)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ z=x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $y=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,1,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=x-1$ (or $x-z+-1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,0,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨0,1,0⟩\\times ⟨1,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $⟨-1,0,-1⟩$ is parallel to the tangent line, then $-⟨-1,0,-1⟩=⟨1,0,1⟩$ is also parallel to it."} :step/id #uuid "a1abbae1-4f02-53d9-a1d3-0117fc214a32" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406833}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406833 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268889 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "106c62f5-6a15-5356-9819-bac29ddd8e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=-4x+9\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266288} {:answer/id #uuid "4cdcc8ed-799e-5868-8d9c-e5cddb211a2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=-4x+21\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266830} {:answer/id #uuid "502e00e2-2746-5fc9-8240-98511ddcf672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=2x+9\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266862} {:answer/id #uuid "50dcaed5-8a14-56a6-9c8d-e4ff85b79e32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=-2x+15\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266872} {:answer/id #uuid "9b80ced7-aa68-5bf4-8dc4-6402f10538d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=2x+21\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267552}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266830} :answer-field/id #uuid "49d228b2-8aea-57a5-b2ca-483e7c7b3e29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268535}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "484f8b36-97b4-5e4f-a875-d05f61c48bf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-132585" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=-2.$ Given that the point $P(4,-2,5)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=y\\sqrt{x}$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=-2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(4,-2,5)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(4,-2)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(4,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(4,-2)} & =(-2)\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =-2(2) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(4,-2)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(4,-2)}(x-4) \\\\ z-5 & =-4(x-4) \\\\ z & =-4x+21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(4,-2,5)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=-4x+21\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a600e828-6ef3-506f-94da-3eafb35c4cfe"}] :activity/title "Geometric Interpretations of Partial Derivatives" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406822}]}
